### (b) Identify the set of potential classes and show clearly how the nouns were rejected using the five rules.

The five rejection rules are applied to identify the suitable classes.

| Noun                 | Decision | Reason                           |
| -------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------- |
| Online bookshop      | Rejected | Represents the entire system     |
| Books                | Accepted | Potential class                  |
| Magazines            | Accepted | Potential class                  |
| CDs                  | Accepted | Potential class                  |
| Products             | Accepted | Common parent class              |
| Price                | Rejected | Attribute of Product             |
| Title                | Rejected | Attribute of Product             |
| Author               | Rejected | Attribute of Book                |
| Number of pages      | Rejected | Attribute of Book                |
| Artists              | Rejected | Attribute of CD                  |
| Type                 | Rejected | Attribute of Product             |
| Customers            | Accepted | Potential class                  |
| Registered customers | Rejected | Redundant with Customers         |
| Personal customers   | Accepted | Type of Customer                 |
| Business customers   | Accepted | Type of Customer                 |
| Orders               | Accepted | Potential class                  |
| Shipments            | Accepted | Potential class                  |
| Store                | Rejected | Irrelevant to the system         |
| Products ordered     | Rejected | Redundant with Product and Order |
| Payments             | Accepted | Potential class                  |
| Credit cards         | Accepted | Represents a payment method      |
| Invoices             | Accepted | Potential class                  |
| Contact information  | Rejected | Attribute of Customer            |
| Personal information | Rejected | Attribute of Customer            |
| Authentication       | Rejected | Represents a process             |
| Delivery             | Rejected | Process represented by Shipment  |
| Reports              | Accepted | Potential class                  |

### Final set of potential classes

After applying the five rejection rules, the identified potential classes are:

1. Product
2. Book
3. Magazine
4. CD
5. Customer
6. PersonalCustomer
7. BusinessCustomer
8. Order
9. Shipment
10. Payment
11. CreditCard
12. Invoice
13. Report
